# Line endings for the files that ship, and for the script that ships them.
# Releases are cut on Windows with core.autocrlf true, which turns LF blobs
# into CRLF in the working copy - and dist/ is copied into the release ZIP
# verbatim. macOS shell scripts must keep LF (see make-release-zip.sh), and
# so must that script itself, since Git Bash chokes on CRLF in a shell file.
*.sh       text eol=lf
*.command  text eol=lf

# Windows scripts keep CRLF.
*.cmd      text eol=crlf
*.bat      text eol=crlf

# Never touched.
*.jar      binary
*.dll      binary
